## What this license does NOT cover, and why

**Third-party literature content.** Paper abstracts, reference lists, and full
texts retrieved from the Semantic Scholar API are not redistributed here. The
Semantic Scholar API License Agreement does not grant us the right to
redistribute publisher-sourced content, and individual records may carry their
own licenses. The release therefore carries identifiers only; refetch the text
yourself under your own API agreement. Semantic Scholar Academic Graph metadata
is distributed by Semantic Scholar under ODC-BY 1.0, and we attribute
Semantic Scholar as that license requires.

**Text generated by the five held-out Gemini models.** The Gemini API
additional terms assign output ownership to the developer but forbid using that
output to develop or improve a competing model. Releasing that text under CC BY
4.0 would purport to grant rights we do not hold, so we do not redistribute it.
For those five models the release carries scores and derived statistics only.

**Model weights.** No model weights are redistributed here. Each model remains
under its own license (Apache-2.0, MIT, Modified MIT, the Gemma Terms of Use,
or the Llama Community License, depending on the family). See the
"Artifact documentation and licensing" appendix of the paper for the per-family
table.

## Intended use

Research on evaluating and improving language-model ideation: reproducing the
published numbers, adding models to the roster, and studying critic behavior.

This data is not a validated instrument for deciding what science to fund or
publish. The hypotheses in it are untested model output, not vetted scientific
claims.
